# Drafted by Gemini (R22 n5), edited.

~ shelf_start
set n5_started
Narrator: Leather book spines tower above you like cliff walls, and grey dust lies drifted ankle-deep like dry snow. Ahead, poor Walter Jenkin stands trapped inside a vast crystal decanter as amber liquor steadily rises around his waist.
nm_golub [sly]: Class is in session, little mice, and today's lesson is how easily a loyal mind drowns in doubt. Sit straight and watch him sink.
nm_wisp [sad]: Leave the bottle be, Walter love, you have done more than enough for this house.
nm_wisp [neutral]: You can go to sleep now, Da. I am right outside on the porch.
nm_wisp [angry]: By the old custom, a servant who cannot speak his mind has no business keeping his head above water.
if not quest.crooked_nightmare >= crooked_bookshelf
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_bookshelf
endif
-> hub

~ hub
if flag.nm_wisp_done and not flag.n5_wisp_counted
set n5_wisp_counted
set walter_loyalty += 3
set n5_clock += 3
Narrator: The colossal cat thins away until only a floating grin remains in the dark, and inside the glass, Walter lifts his chin.
-> tick
endif
Narrator: The heavy glass stopper presses down over Walter's head while the dark spirits swirl around his knees.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Rally Walter, tell him Dani needs him -> rally_ok | rally_fail
* [Intimidation DC 20] Bellow for him to stand up -> rally_ok | rally_fail
* [History DC 20] Remind him that dreams lie -> rally_ok | rally_fail
* [Nature DC 20] Reason that a dream cannot drown a man -> rally_ok | rally_fail
* [Deception DC 20] Distract Wisp with a grand lie -> rally_ok | rally_fail
* [if not flag.nm_wisp_done] Fight Wisp -> fight_wisp
* [if not flag.golub_struck] Strike Golub -> golub_hit
* [if not flag.n5_plain_told] Say it plainly: Dani is waiting for him -> plain
* [if item:dani_lantern and not flag.n5_lantern_shown] Hold Dani's lantern up to the glass -> lantern_show
* Hold fast and wait a round -> wait
* Hear Golub out -> golub_talk
* Step back for a moment -> END

~ rally_ok
Narrator: Your call cuts cleanly through the thick crystal. Walter scrawls a quick note, presses the paper flat against the wet glass: I hear you, I am holding fast: and squares his shoulders.
set walter_loyalty += 1
-> tick

~ rally_fail
Narrator: Your words seem to skate off the curved glass without reaching him, drowned out by the purring dark. Walter bows his head a fraction lower.
-> tick

~ plain
Narrator: You press your hands to the cold glass and say it with no tricks in it: Dani is on the porch, and she is waiting. Walter reads your lips, and something in his shoulders settles.
set n5_plain_told
set walter_loyalty += 1
-> tick

~ lantern_show
Narrator: The blue mist behind Dani's lantern glass leans toward the decanter like a cat toward a hand. Walter sees it, and knows whose it is.
set n5_lantern_shown
set walter_loyalty += 1
-> tick

~ wait
Narrator: There is nothing to do but hold fast and watch the liquor climb another notch, and hope someone in the glass is counting.
-> tick

~ fight_wisp
Narrator: Great velvet paws the size of hay-wagons sweep across the dusty shelf as the cat lunges in.
combat nm_wisp

~ golub_hit
nm_golub [angry]: Rude little beetles, striking your own schoolmistress before the bell has rung.
Narrator: Your blow passes through her pleated skirt, and she bursts into a dry scatter of grey pigeon feathers.
vanish nm_golub
set golub_struck
-> hub

~ golub_talk
nm_golub [sly]: Stonoga only knows how to baste flesh, and Vessla fusses over souls with her tin sword. I am the one who cracks a mind open with quiet shame until it begs for the knife.
nm_golub [smile]: Look at him in the amber dark, half-convinced he already failed his girl.
-> hub

~ tick
set n5_clock += 1
Narrator: Another heavy measure of spiced liquor wells up from the bottom of the decanter, climbing higher up Walter's coat.
if flag.walter_loyalty >= 6
-> freed
endif
if flag.n5_clock >= 10
-> drowned
endif
-> hub

~ freed
Narrator: Walter braces his boots against the slick glass walls and drives both hands upward, heaving the massive crystal stopper clean out of the neck. The pigeon-hag's shadow scatters, the great cat fades to a bare grin, and a cool blue mist curls down to lift Walter gently out of the dream.
cutscene nm_pulled_out
Narrator: A hand of blue mist closes round a hand, and the captive is drawn up and out of the dream.
cutscene nm_pulled_out_2
Narrator: Far away on the porch, Dani keeps her eyes shut, and a thread of blue light runs from her hands into the house.
cutscene end
vanish walter_jenkin
set walter_saved
set nm_shelf_done
-> voices_drop

~ drowned
Narrator: The dark amber tide closes quietly over Walter's grey head, and his hands slip down from the inside of the glass. The bubbles rise, slow and silver, until the decanter is still.
set walter_dead
set nm_shelf_done
-> voices_drop

~ voices_drop
Narrator: A sudden rain of tiny glass thimbles patters down from where the cat's mouth hung, rolling across the dusty wood and humming softly with stolen voices. Inside the floating grin, the outline of a crooked red door begins to glow.
set nm_voices_dropped
quest voices_not_their_own asked
-> END

~ door
if not flag.nm_shelf_done
Narrator: For now, the floating grin is only a row of gleaming teeth hanging in the dark beyond the shelf.
-> END
endif
Narrator: The crooked red door shimmers between the cat's lingering rows of ivory teeth, smelling faintly of sweet wine and catnip.
* [if not (quest.voices_not_their_own == asked or quest.voices_not_their_own == listening)] Step through the grin -> toll
* [if not (quest.voices_not_their_own == asked or quest.voices_not_their_own == listening)] [Performance DC 12] Tell the grin a joke -> joke_ok | joke_fail
* [if quest.voices_not_their_own == asked or quest.voices_not_their_own == listening] [ends:voices_not_their_own] Leave the thimbles behind and step through the grin -> leave_voices
* Not yet -> END

~ joke_ok
Narrator: The wide mouth quivers at the punchline, lets out a wheezing giggle, and its sharp teeth go soft as tallow.
set dream_laughed
-> toll

~ joke_fail
Narrator: The disembodied mouth widens politely at your effort, though the fangs stay just as keen as before.
-> toll

~ toll
if flag.dream_laughed
Narrator: Still chuckling to itself, the grinning doorway forgets to snap shut as you slip across the threshold.
set dream_laughed = false
-> pass
endif
check Dexterity DC 17 -> pass | toll_hurt

~ toll_hurt
Narrator: The rows of teeth snap together as you dive through, catching at your cloak and flesh before you tumble out the other side.
damage 2d10 slashing
-> pass

~ leave_voices
Narrator: You leave the thimbles humming on the shelf. Behind you, one by one, they stop.
quest voices_not_their_own lost
set voices_outcome = "lost"
-> toll

~ pass
if not quest.crooked_nightmare >= wedding_feast
quest crooked_nightmare wedding_feast
endif
move nm_wedding
